# Brave. Not in Debian.
#
# Brave publishes a third-party APT repository, and that is the route their own
# documentation gives. Strata does not use it: an APT signing key is trusted for
# every package name, including replacements for system components, so adding
# one is a systemwide grant rather than installing an application. Flathub can
# offer applications and nothing more, which is the weaker and therefore correct
# permission here. See ADR-0011.
SUMMARY="Brave, a Chromium-based browser with built-in blocking"
CATEGORY="browser"
ORIGIN="flatpak"
SOURCE="Flathub (flathub.org)"
PACKAGES="flatpak"
FLATPAK_REF="com.brave.Browser"
DESKTOP="com.brave.Browser.desktop"
NOTE="The first Flatpak application also pulls a runtime, so expect a larger download than the browser alone."
